    {
      "name": "fractional_negative_truncates_toward_zero",
      "why": "truncation must be toward ZERO, not floor -- and the CLOCK is what makes that checkable. trunc(-1.5) is -1 and floor(-1.5) is -2, so only a `now` BETWEEN them tells the two apart: at now = -2, truncation leaves the token valid and flooring expires it. At now = 0 both expire it and the case asserts nothing, which is what the first draft of this vector did",
      "exp": -1.5,
