    {
      "name": "boolean_false",
      "why": "the falsy twin -- and the CLOCK is what gives it teeth. At now = 0 the coercing rule refuses it too (`0 >= false` is `0 >= 0`, expired) and the case asserts nothing; the first draft ran it there and claimed it blocked a 'reject truthy non-numbers' fix, which it did not. At now = -1 the coercion ACCEPTS it and only a real type rule refuses it",
      "exp": false,
      "exp_absent": false,
      "now_s": -1,
